msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:182
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.background_help"
msgid "Field map is a tool that enable users to view the physical layout of plots in a trial. Maps can be generated on the fly while adding a trial or uploading a trial. Field map coordinates can also be uploaded independently after trials have been added or uploaded. It is a very intuitive, flexible and user friendly tool for manipulation/making changes to field trial layouts before phenotypes are uploaded."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:203
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.borders_help"
msgid "These checkboxes allow you to add borders around your field map on any sides you would like. These plots are purely visual and have no real data associated with them. They will not be included in the database, but you can see them in your harvesting order if they are present."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:226
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.delete_map_help"
msgid "Field Map can be deleted if the user have the right privilege."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:193
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.dimensions_help"
msgid "Click on the change dimensions button to alter the dimensions of the field map, and the respective row and column attributes of the plots in your trial. Clicking on this button will open a dialogue that prompts you to enter an accession name if the change you are making will result in dimensions that are larger than the amount of plots in your trial. The result is that the map will fill in the extra space with filler plots, and the filler plots will have the accession entered in input in the dialogue."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:222
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.double_click_help"
msgid "Double clicking on a plot, opens the stock page for that plot."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:224
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.download_map_help"
msgid "Field Map can be downloaded as image using the download button below the map."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:199
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.harvest_help"
msgid "This button allows you to download an excel file which has an incrementally ordered list of the harvesting order for your trial based on the current layout of the field map. You can play around with the four options given to experiment with the different traversal patterns available. The harvesting order file will omit border plots, but it will include filler plots."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:207
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.heatmap_help"
msgid "If your trial has trait data uploaded, you can view a heatmap of that data by selecting a trait from the dropdown menu. You will see a color weighting on the plots that corresponds with the value of each plot for a given trait."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:195
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.invert_help"
msgid "Check invert rows to observe your trial from the top down instead of the bottom up. This change is only present on your visualization, and the trial data will not be changed."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:197
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.layout_help"
msgid "You can select how you want your map to be ordered. The options include serpentine and zigzag."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:220
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.mouse_over_help"
msgid "Displays plot field information."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:233
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.phenotype_lock_note"
msgid "- <b>Changes can only be made to the physical layout when phenotypes are not yet upload for the trial.</b>"
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:201
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.plant_help"
msgid "This button allows you to download an excel file which has an incrementally ordered list of the planting order for your trial. It is very similar to the harvesting order, but since you will need to plant the borders too, it includes the border plots in the traversal of your map."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:189
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.replace_plot_help"
msgid "A plot accession can be replaced by an accession within or outside of the trial. To do this, <b>click on the plot</b> and <b>provide the name of the new accession</b> (must already exist in the database)."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:191
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.replace_trial_help"
msgid "An accession used in a trial can be replaced by a new accession or another accession from the trial. When this replace option is used, it replaces every instances (plots and plants) of that accession in the trial. To do this, <b>click on the Edit Field Map link</b> by the top right of the physical trial layout section; <b>click on Replace Accession button</b>; <b>select accession</b> to replace from the trial and <b>provide a new accession</b> (must already exit in the database); <b>click on Replace Trial Accession button</b> to complete the operation."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:231
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.roles_note"
msgid "- You have to be a <b>curator</b> or a <b>submitter and associated to the breeding program</b> of the trial to use the features of this tool."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:205
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.submit_help"
msgid "This button allows you to update the databases with the changes you have made to your trial. You can continuously change your trial data, just remember to submit the changes when you are satisfied so that it is saved."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/trial/edit_fieldMap.mas:209
msgctxt "trial.fieldmap_edit.help.transpose_help"
msgid "This button transposes the x and y coordinates of each plot in your map. Borders will adjust accordingly."
msgstr ""

